// A question that is answered, after which the agent says nothing at all.
//
// The silence is the whole scenario. Everywhere else the agent goes on talking
// once it has its answer, and every update it sends republishes the attachment
// — so a client that failed to publish when the answer was taken would still
// look right by the time anyone read it, masked by the next chunk. Here nothing
// follows the answer, so the attachment can only show what answering itself
// published.
//
// The turn is deliberately left running. What is being proved is the state a
// host would poll while it waits, not how the turn ends.
